.TH tuterm n 0.1 tclutils
.SH tclutils::tuterm
.PP
ANSI terminal styling (SGR): text attributes and 16\- / 256\- / 24\-bit colors, with a global enable switch (honouring the \fBNO_COLOR\fR convention), an ANSI stripper, and optional Windows VT\-mode initialisation. Pure Tcl, GUI\-free.
.SS Package
.CS
package require tclutils::tuterm 0.1
.CE
.SS Commands
.CS
::tclutils::tuterm::style ?spec ...?       ;# -> SGR sequence ("" when disabled)
::tclutils::tuterm::wrap  text ?spec ...?   ;# -> styled text + reset
::tclutils::tuterm::off   attr              ;# -> the "off" SGR for one attribute
::tclutils::tuterm::names ?what?            ;# -> available names
::tclutils::tuterm::strip text              ;# -> text with SGR removed
::tclutils::tuterm::enable ?bool?           ;# -> get/set global enable flag
::tclutils::tuterm::auto                    ;# -> set enable from NO_COLOR
::tclutils::tuterm::enableVT                ;# -> Windows VT mode (no-op elsewhere)
::tclutils::tuterm::disableVT
.CE
.SS "Style specs"
.PP
Accepted by \fBstyle\fR and \fBwrap\fR:
.TS
l l.
Spec	Meaning
\fBreset\fR	reset all attributes
\fBbold\fR \fBdim\fR \fBitalic\fR \fBunderline\fR \fBblink\fR \fBreverse\fR \fBinvisible\fR \fBstrike\fR	turn the attribute \fBon\fR
\fBbold:on\fR / \fBbold:off\fR (any attribute)	turn explicitly on/off
\fBfg:<color>\fR / \fBbg:<color>\fR	foreground / background color
.TE
.PP
\fB<color>\fR is a name (\fBred\fR, \fBbright_cyan\fR, …), a 256\-color index \fB0..255\fR, or a \fB#rrggbb\fR truecolor value. \fBfgcolor:\fR / \fBbgcolor:\fR are accepted as aliases.
.SS Usage
.CS
package require tclutils::tuterm
namespace import ::tclutils::tuterm::*

puts [wrap "Important!" bold fg:red]
puts "[style fg:yellow]warning[style reset]"
puts [wrap "ok" fg:#00aa00]          ;# truecolor
puts [wrap "note" fg:208]            ;# 256-color
.CE
.PP
Disable color for pipes / \fBNO_COLOR\fR:
.CS
::tclutils::tuterm::auto             ;# disables if NO_COLOR is set
# or force:
::tclutils::tuterm::enable 0
.CE
.PP
On Windows, enable VT processing once at startup so escapes render:
.CS
::tclutils::tuterm::enableVT         ;# needs twapi; no-op on other platforms
.CE
.PP
\fBstrip\fR removes SGR sequences (e.g. before measuring width or logging):
.CS
string length [::tclutils::tuterm::strip $styled]
.CE
.SS Notes
.IP \(bu
When disabled, \fBstyle\fR returns \fB""\fR and \fBwrap\fR returns the plain text, so the same code paths work with or without color.
.IP \(bu
\fBenableVT\fR uses \fBtwapi\fR if present; it returns 1 on success or on non\-Windows platforms, 0 only if the Windows call failed.
.SS "Error codes"
.PP
\fB\-errorcode {TCLUTILS TUTERM <REASON>}\fR (\fBSTYLE\fR, \fBVALUE\fR, \fBCATEGORY\fR).
